{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-35222","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53553","text":"Portable Subject-Mode Closure — memo"}]},{"id":"blk-35223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53554","marks":["bold"],"text":"Slice:"},{"id":"spn-53555","text":" the correction ruled onto the top of the identity ladder, not a new rung. "},{"id":"spn-53556","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-53557","text":" shipped."}]},{"id":"blk-35224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53558","marks":["bold"],"text":"Battery."},{"id":"spn-53559","text":" D31–D40 with the engine present: "},{"id":"spn-53560","marks":["bold"],"text":"10 passed / 0 skipped / 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-53561","text":"; engine absent: "},{"id":"spn-53562","marks":["bold"],"text":"4 passed / 6 skipped / 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-53563","text":" (D32, D37, D38 and D40 are recipient-side laws and need no Forge checkout — see §3). D1–D40: "},{"id":"spn-53564","marks":["bold"],"text":"40/40"},{"id":"spn-53565","text":" engine present, 16/24 engine absent. Whole tree: "},{"id":"spn-53566","marks":["bold"],"text":"474 passed / 0 skipped / 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-53567","text":" across 26 files."}]},{"id":"blk-35225","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53568","text":"Ruled by the sixth GPT-5.6 ruling, which accepted "},{"id":"spn-53569","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-53570","text":" and then reproduced the caveat §6 of the previous memo had flagged:"}]},{"id":"blk-35226","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"source file mode:       0664\nmanifest mode:          0644\nbundle verification:    passes\ncanonical ZIP extract:  0644\nsame bundle_id:         yes          ← and yet\ndifferent snap-:        yes          ← so a different env-"},{"id":"blk-35227","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"pack directory        → bundle verifies, environment verifies\narchive-bundle        → normalizes 0664 → 0644\nextract archive       → bundle still verifies, environment FAILS to reopen"},{"id":"blk-35228","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53571","text":"It ruled that a reachable correctness defect, not an acceptable residual, and ordered it closed now."}]},{"id":"blk-35229","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53572","text":"1. Why the previous slice was wrong to ship it as a caveat"}]},{"id":"blk-35230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53573","text":"Both halves of the tension were individually correct and I could not see a way to weaken either, so I recorded the residual and moved on. That was the error. The residual is not a "},{"id":"spn-53574","marks":["italic"],"text":"tension between two identities"},{"id":"spn-53575","text":" — it is a "},{"id":"spn-53576","marks":["bold"],"text":"package that cannot survive its own archive"},{"id":"spn-53577","text":", and neither identity has to move to say so. The fix lives in a third place: "},{"id":"spn-53578","marks":["bold"],"text":"admission"},{"id":"spn-53579","text":". A mode that cannot be transported is refused before either id is minted."}]},{"id":"blk-35231","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53580","text":"Stated the other way round: "},{"id":"spn-53581","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-53582","text":" sealing the exact mode is a claim about a repository, and "},{"id":"spn-53583","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-53584","text":" carrying the canonical mode is a claim about a distribution. There is no contradiction, only a set of repositories that are not distributable. TRAAVIIS packages distributions. So that set is inadmissible."}]},{"id":"blk-35232","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53585","text":"2. What was built"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-35234","spans":[{"id":"spn-53586","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-35235","spans":[{"id":"spn-53587","text":"change"}]}],"id":"blk-35233","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-35236","spans":[{"id":"spn-53588","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/substrates.py"}]},{"id":"blk-35237","spans":[{"id":"spn-53589","marks":["code"],"text":"CANONICAL_SUBJECT_MODES"},{"id":"spn-53590","text":", "},{"id":"spn-53591","marks":["code"],"text":"canonical_subject_mode"},{"id":"spn-53592","text":", "},{"id":"spn-53593","marks":["code"],"text":"require_canonical_subject_modes"},{"id":"spn-53594","text":"; called from "},{"id":"spn-53595","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-53596","text":" Residency seams."}]}],[{"id":"blk-35238","spans":[{"id":"spn-53597","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/bundle.py"}]},{"id":"blk-35239","spans":[{"id":"spn-53598","marks":["code"],"text":"write_archive"},{"id":"spn-53599","text":" gated on a serialized round trip; new "},{"id":"spn-53600","marks":["code"],"text":"_verify_serialized"},{"id":"spn-53601","text":"; new refusal "},{"id":"spn-53602","marks":["code"],"text":"BUNDLE_ARCHIVE_ROUNDTRIP"},{"id":"spn-53603","text":"; report gains "},{"id":"spn-53604","marks":["code"],"text":"roundtrip_verified"},{"id":"spn-53605","text":"."}]}],[{"id":"blk-35240","spans":[{"id":"spn-53606","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/scaffold.py"}]},{"id":"blk-35241","spans":[{"id":"spn-53607","marks":["code"],"text":"SCAFFOLD_FILE_MODE"},{"id":"spn-53608","text":"; every scaffolded file written at an explicit "},{"id":"spn-53609","marks":["code"],"text":"0644"},{"id":"spn-53610","text":"."}]}],[{"id":"blk-35242","spans":[{"id":"spn-53611","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/cli.py"}]},{"id":"blk-35243","spans":[{"id":"spn-53612","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-53613","text":" relabels the legacy field "},{"id":"spn-53614","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"episode evidence\""},{"id":"spn-53615","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-53616","marks":["code"],"text":"archive-bundle"},{"id":"spn-53617","text":" prints the round-trip line."}]}],[{"id":"blk-35244","spans":[{"id":"spn-53618","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/evalsplit.py"}]},{"id":"blk-35245","spans":[{"id":"spn-53619","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1.bundle"},{"id":"spn-53620","text":" documented as a legacy episode-member field with a frozen value law."}]}],[{"id":"blk-35246","spans":[{"id":"spn-53621","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_bundle.py"}]},{"id":"blk-35247","spans":[{"id":"spn-53622","text":"D31–D40."}]}],[{"id":"blk-35248","spans":[{"id":"spn-53623","marks":["code"],"text":"RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md"}]},{"id":"blk-35249","spans":[{"id":"spn-53624","text":"new "},{"id":"spn-53625","marks":["bold"],"text":"§5c"},{"id":"spn-53626","text":" freezes both laws; §5b gains the "},{"id":"spn-53627","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1.bundle"},{"id":"spn-53628","text":" paragraph."}]}],[{"id":"blk-35250","spans":[{"id":"spn-53629","marks":["code"],"text":"README.md"}]},{"id":"blk-35251","spans":[{"id":"spn-53630","text":"archive publication, a subject-mode section, and the legacy-field note."}]}]]},{"id":"blk-35252","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53631","text":"The admission law"}]},{"id":"blk-35253","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53632","text":"For "},{"id":"spn-53633","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-53634","text":", every file whose mode enters "},{"id":"spn-53635","marks":["code"],"text":"SnapshotV1.file_modes"},{"id":"spn-53636","text":" must already be exactly "},{"id":"spn-53637","marks":["code"],"text":"0644"},{"id":"spn-53638","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-53639","marks":["code"],"text":"0755"},{"id":"spn-53640","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-35254","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\"paths\": {\"src/tool.py\": {\"observed\": \"0664\", \"required\": \"0644\"}}}"},{"id":"blk-35255","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53641","text":"typed "},{"id":"spn-53642","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SUBJECT_MODE_NONCANONICAL`"},{"id":"spn-53643","text":", raised from one shared helper called by "},{"id":"spn-53644","marks":["code"],"text":"recompute_subject_identity"},{"id":"spn-53645","text":" (authoring) and "},{"id":"spn-53646","marks":["code"],"text":"_reopen_subject"},{"id":"spn-53647","text":" (reopening, therefore also "},{"id":"spn-53648","marks":["code"],"text":"reopen_package"},{"id":"spn-53649","text":" and therefore "},{"id":"spn-53650","marks":["code"],"text":"verify_bundle"},{"id":"spn-53651","text":"). That covers all three ways a nonportable package can appear: authored here, hand-built elsewhere, or authored before the law existed."}]},{"id":"blk-35256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53652","text":"The helper reads "},{"id":"spn-53653","marks":["code"],"text":"SnapshotV1.file_modes"},{"id":"spn-53654","text":" rather than walking the tree. That is the whole of D35: "},{"id":"spn-53655","marks":["code"],"text":"file_modes"},{"id":"spn-53656","text":" is already post-exclusion and already symlink-free, so an excluded file is out of scope "},{"id":"spn-53657","marks":["bold"],"text":"by construction"},{"id":"spn-53658","text":" rather than by a second glob match that could drift away from the first."}]},{"id":"blk-35257","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53659","marks":["code"],"text":"f\"{mode:04o}\""},{"id":"spn-53660","text":" renders set-ID modes as "},{"id":"spn-53661","marks":["code"],"text":"4755"},{"id":"spn-53662","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-53663","marks":["code"],"text":"2755"},{"id":"spn-53664","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-53665","marks":["code"],"text":"1644"},{"id":"spn-53666","text":", which are outside a two-element allowlist and are therefore refused without needing to be enumerated. The law is stated as an allowlist for exactly that reason."}]},{"id":"blk-35258","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53667","text":"The archive publication law"}]},{"id":"blk-35259","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"verify source tree\n→ write a temporary archive\n→ extract it to a temporary directory\n→ verify bundle closure from the extracted bytes\n→ when not --package-only, re-derive env- and subject closure too\n→ compare bundle_id and env_id\n→ atomically publish"},{"id":"blk-35260","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53668","text":"The old order verified the "},{"id":"spn-53669","marks":["italic"],"text":"directory"},{"id":"spn-53670","text":" and then serialized it, which proves the directory — not the artifact anyone receives. Anything serialization normalizes away was invisible to it, which is precisely how the mode defect could reach a published archive. A failed round trip raises "},{"id":"spn-53671","marks":["code"],"text":"BUNDLE_ARCHIVE_ROUNDTRIP"},{"id":"spn-53672","text":" and leaves no archive at the output path."}]},{"id":"blk-35261","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53673","text":"3. D31–D40"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-35263","spans":[{"id":"spn-53674","text":"#"}]},{"id":"blk-35264","spans":[{"id":"spn-53675","text":"law"}]},{"id":"blk-35265","spans":[{"id":"spn-53676","text":"test"}]}],"id":"blk-35262","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-35266","spans":[{"id":"spn-53677","text":"D31"}]},{"id":"blk-35267","spans":[{"id":"spn-53678","text":"a Residency subject mode "},{"id":"spn-53679","marks":["code"],"text":"0664"},{"id":"spn-53680","text":" is refused"}]},{"id":"blk-35268","spans":[{"id":"spn-53681","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d31_a_noncanonical_residency_subject_mode_is_refused"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35269","spans":[{"id":"spn-53682","text":"D32"}]},{"id":"blk-35270","spans":[{"id":"spn-53683","marks":["code"],"text":"0600"},{"id":"spn-53684","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-53685","marks":["code"],"text":"0640"},{"id":"spn-53686","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-53687","marks":["code"],"text":"0775"},{"id":"spn-53688","text":" / set-ID modes are refused too"}]},{"id":"blk-35271","spans":[{"id":"spn-53689","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d32_every_other_noncanonical_mode_is_refused_too"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35272","spans":[{"id":"spn-53690","text":"D33"}]},{"id":"blk-35273","spans":[{"id":"spn-53691","text":"canonical "},{"id":"spn-53692","marks":["code"],"text":"0644"},{"id":"spn-53693","text":" subjects survive directory→ZIP→extract→verify"}]},{"id":"blk-35274","spans":[{"id":"spn-53694","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d33_canonical_0644_subjects_survive_directory_zip_extract_verify"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35275","spans":[{"id":"spn-53695","text":"D34"}]},{"id":"blk-35276","spans":[{"id":"spn-53696","text":"canonical "},{"id":"spn-53697","marks":["code"],"text":"0755"},{"id":"spn-53698","text":" subjects survive the same path"}]},{"id":"blk-35277","spans":[{"id":"spn-53699","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d34_canonical_0755_subjects_survive_the_same_path"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35278","spans":[{"id":"spn-53700","text":"D35"}]},{"id":"blk-35279","spans":[{"id":"spn-53701","text":"excluded files' modes do not affect admission"}]},{"id":"blk-35280","spans":[{"id":"spn-53702","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d35_excluded_files_with_noncanonical_modes_do_not_affect_admission"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35281","spans":[{"id":"spn-53703","text":"D36"}]},{"id":"blk-35282","spans":[{"id":"spn-53704","text":"presentation modes may normalize without moving "},{"id":"spn-53705","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"}]},{"id":"blk-35283","spans":[{"id":"spn-53706","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d36_presentation_modes_may_normalize_without_moving_the_environment"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35284","spans":[{"id":"spn-53707","text":"D37"}]},{"id":"blk-35285","spans":[{"id":"spn-53708","text":"publication verifies the extracted archive before rename"}]},{"id":"blk-35286","spans":[{"id":"spn-53709","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d37_archive_publication_verifies_the_extracted_archive_before_rename"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35287","spans":[{"id":"spn-53710","text":"D38"}]},{"id":"blk-35288","spans":[{"id":"spn-53711","text":"a failed round trip leaves no final archive"}]},{"id":"blk-35289","spans":[{"id":"spn-53712","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d38_a_failed_archive_roundtrip_leaves_no_final_archive"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35290","spans":[{"id":"spn-53713","text":"D39"}]},{"id":"blk-35291","spans":[{"id":"spn-53714","text":"ZIP and tar full "},{"id":"spn-53715","marks":["italic"],"text":"environment"},{"id":"spn-53716","text":" verification agree"}]},{"id":"blk-35292","spans":[{"id":"spn-53717","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d39_zip_and_tar_full_environment_verification_agree"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35293","spans":[{"id":"spn-53718","text":"D40"}]},{"id":"blk-35294","spans":[{"id":"spn-53719","text":"D1–D30 and the packet gates remain green"}]},{"id":"blk-35295","spans":[{"id":"spn-53720","marks":["code"],"text":"test_d40_the_earlier_laws_and_the_packet_gates_are_untouched"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-35296","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53721","text":"D31 additionally proves both non-authoring seams: a hand-built package whose seal is "},{"id":"spn-53722","marks":["italic"],"text":"self-consistent"},{"id":"spn-53723","text":" at "},{"id":"spn-53724","marks":["code"],"text":"0664"},{"id":"spn-53725","text":" is refused at reopen, and a scaffold written under "},{"id":"spn-53726","marks":["code"],"text":"umask 002"},{"id":"spn-53727","text":" still packs (see §4)."}]},{"id":"blk-35297","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53728","text":"D37 is observed at the publication seam — it spies "},{"id":"spn-53729","marks":["code"],"text":"verify_bundle"},{"id":"spn-53730","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-53731","marks":["code"],"text":"os.replace"},{"id":"spn-53732","text":" and asserts that everything verified before publication was an "},{"id":"spn-53733","marks":["bold"],"text":"extraction"},{"id":"spn-53734","text":", never the source directory. D38 drives both failure modes: a closure failure out of the extraction, and a round trip that verifies cleanly as some "},{"id":"spn-53735","marks":["italic"],"text":"other"},{"id":"spn-53736","text":" package, which is the branch that catches silent normalization."}]},{"id":"blk-35298","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53737","text":"D40 is a completeness check, not a re-run: D1–D30 are re-run by the battery itself, in the same process, every time. What D40 asserts is that no earlier law was dropped or renamed (the D-numbers are exactly 1..40), that the source-release gate learned nothing about either new code, and that "},{"id":"spn-53738","marks":["code"],"text":"TrvmWorldV1"},{"id":"spn-53739","text":" did "},{"id":"spn-53740","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-53741","text":" inherit the mode law while "},{"id":"spn-53742","marks":["code"],"text":"ResidencyRepositoryV1"},{"id":"spn-53743","text":" enforces it at exactly two seams."}]},{"id":"blk-35299","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53744","text":"4. A defect this slice created and then closed"}]},{"id":"blk-35300","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53745","text":"Adding the admission law immediately broke "},{"id":"spn-53746","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs init"},{"id":"spn-53747","text":" on any machine with a loose umask. "},{"id":"spn-53748","marks":["code"],"text":"scaffold.materialize"},{"id":"spn-53749","text":" wrote every file at the process umask default, so under "},{"id":"spn-53750","marks":["code"],"text":"umask 002"},{"id":"spn-53751","text":" a freshly scaffolded environment is "},{"id":"spn-53752","marks":["code"],"text":"0664"},{"id":"spn-53753","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-53754","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs pack"},{"id":"spn-53755","text":" now — correctly — refuses it. Every author on a "},{"id":"spn-53756","marks":["code"],"text":"002"},{"id":"spn-53757","text":" machine would have been locked out by their first two commands."}]},{"id":"blk-35301","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53758","text":"It was invisible here only because this machine runs "},{"id":"spn-53759","marks":["code"],"text":"umask 022"},{"id":"spn-53760","text":", so the default coincided with the declared mode. Exactly the same shape as the latent defect the previous slice closed, from exactly the same cause: a template's modes are part of the template, and were being taken from the machine that unpacked it."}]},{"id":"blk-35302","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53761","text":"Closed by writing every scaffolded file at an explicit "},{"id":"spn-53762","marks":["code"],"text":"SCAFFOLD_FILE_MODE = 0o644"},{"id":"spn-53763","text":" (and the scaffold root at "},{"id":"spn-53764","marks":["code"],"text":"0755"},{"id":"spn-53765","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-53766","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-53767","text":" under a restrictive umask does not emit a "},{"id":"spn-53768","marks":["code"],"text":"0700"},{"id":"spn-53769","text":" environment either). D31 pins it with a real "},{"id":"spn-53770","marks":["code"],"text":"os.umask(0o002)"},{"id":"spn-53771","text":" scaffold that must still pack to the reference "},{"id":"spn-53772","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-53773","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-35303","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53774","text":"5. "},{"id":"spn-53775","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV1.bundle"},{"id":"spn-53776","text":" — kept, relabelled"}]},{"id":"blk-35304","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53777","text":"Ruled: do "},{"id":"spn-53778","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-53779","text":" rename it. Done, and the strengthened D27 reading was confirmed correct. What changed is only ambiguity:"}]},{"id":"blk-35305","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35307","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53780","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval-one"},{"id":"spn-53781","text":" prints "},{"id":"spn-53782","marks":["bold"],"text":"`episode evidence: …`"},{"id":"spn-53783","text":", on both the human and the"}]}],"id":"blk-35306","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53784","marks":["code"],"text":"--json"},{"id":"spn-53785","text":" stderr line. It no longer prints the word \"bundle\" for this field."}]},{"id":"blk-35309","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35311","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53786","marks":["code"],"text":"evalsplit.py"},{"id":"spn-53787","text":" documents it as a "},{"id":"spn-53788","marks":["bold"],"text":"legacy episode-member field"},{"id":"spn-53789","text":" with a frozen"}]}],"id":"blk-35310","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53790","text":"value law: "},{"id":"spn-53791","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-53792","text":", or exactly one "},{"id":"spn-53793","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-<id>"},{"id":"spn-53794","text":" directory name."}]},{"id":"blk-35313","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35315","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53795","text":"RFC §5b and the README say the same, and both name "},{"id":"spn-53796","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV2"},{"id":"spn-53797","text":" →"}]}],"id":"blk-35314","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53798","marks":["code"],"text":"episode_member"},{"id":"spn-53799","text":" as the eventual rename."}]},{"id":"blk-35317","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35319","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53800","text":"No "},{"id":"spn-53801","marks":["code"],"text":"EvaluationV2"},{"id":"spn-53802","text":" was introduced."}]}],"id":"blk-35318","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35320","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53803","text":"D27 remains the enforcement: no "},{"id":"spn-53804","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle_id"},{"id":"spn-53805","text":" key and no "},{"id":"spn-53806","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-53807","text":" value anywhere, "},{"id":"spn-53808","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-53809","text":" every surviving "},{"id":"spn-53810","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle"},{"id":"spn-53811","text":" field must hold an "},{"id":"spn-53812","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-53813","text":" directory."}]},{"id":"blk-35321","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53814","text":"6. Autonomous decisions (flagged for review)"}]},{"id":"blk-35322","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35324","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53815","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-53816","